A||||5||Jay||348 kit for the fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||05-15-2001||02:06 PM||||I just finished reading the new Forza magazine (all Ferrari).  I realized that the 348's are significantly shorter than the 308 and 328's that preceeded it.  Hence the 348 would make a better kit for the Fiero.  The overall length of the car would be more accurate than a 308 or 328.  That is something that has always buged me about 308/328 kits.  Is there a 348 kit already made for the Fiero?  Of all my years of owning Fiero's and kits I've never seen one.  Apparently, the real 348's body panels can be exchanged (with some exception) with the 355.  Anybody out there have a 348 kit for the Fiero?<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wade87GT||05-15-2001||07:50 PM||||I've been watching the kit car thing for years and haven't seen any 348 kits yet. Since the 348 body style is one of the least desireable of the Ferraris (if there is such a thing) I don't expect much of a market for a rebody. I've always thought it looked like a wide-body Fiero GT anyway. Maybe Ferrari copied the IMSA Fiero fastback   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. A key point to measure, for accurate kit purposes, is the distance from the firewall to the center of the rear wheel opening. Remember, the 348's engine is mounted longitudinally. I get Forza too and that 348 looked perfect in black!<p>[This message has been edited by Wade87GT (edited 05-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-15-2001||07:51 PM||||original 308/328 are only an inch different in wheelbase than Fiero. fiero is 93.4'', 328 is 92.5 ''. I bought a custom fit California Car Cover for a 308/328 and it fits my car like a glove. The 348 is 96.4, so it would need a 3 inch stretch.You can find all the specs for all Ferraris here. its also just a neat site to explore.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ferrarina.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ferrarina.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">   <P>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-15-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-15-2001).]||||reg||1
